From {{etyl|gem-pro|goh}} {{recons|habjaną|lang=gem-pro}}, whence also Old Saxon {{term|hebbian|lang=osx}}, Old English {{term|habban|lang=ang}}, Old Norse {{term|hafa|lang=non}}, Gothic {{term|𐌷𐌰𐌱𐌰𐌽|tr=haban|lang=got}}. Ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|goh}} {{recons|keh₂p-||to grasp|lang=ine-pro}}, whence also Latin {{term|capio|capiō|lang=la}}.

===Verb===
{{head|goh|verb|head=habēn}}

# to [[have]]

